--TEST--
A loop that only echoes stops at the first write past `[limits] max_output`, with a limit report naming `max_output` — `rule:errors/on-limit`
--FILE nvs.toml--
# The run may write 25 bytes.
[limits]
max_output = "25"
--FILE--
<?nvs
Core\Fatal::onLimit(fn (array<string> $report): void => {
    echo "onLimit ", $report['limit'], "\n";
});

// Each line is 10 bytes. The third line takes the total to 30 bytes, so the
// loop stops before the fourth.
for (var $i = 0; $i < 1000; $i++) {
    echo "line ", $i, "...\n";
}
--EXPECT--
line 0...
line 1...
line 2...
onLimit max_output
--EXPECT-ERROR--
FATAL: the request exceeded its output limit — 30 bytes written by the request and everything it spawned, against a ceiling of 25
